<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="10">
<name>Body &amp; Electrical</name>
<section id="1002S_S000E" variety="S000E">
<name>Vehicle Surroundings Monitor</name>
<ttl id="1002S_S000E_746W2_T00DG" variety="T00DG">
<name>Back Guide Monitor System</name>
<para id="RM000003NC100NX" category="J" type-id="80410" name-id="673A4-01" from="200912">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>"Back Door Is Open. Close Back Door Before Use" Is Displayed Even When Back Door Is Closed</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000003NC100NX_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HYW00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The navigation receiver assembly receives the back door open/close signal of the back door lock assembly from the instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU) via CAN communication. Since the television camera assembly is installed on the back door, accurate camera optical axis adjustment cannot be performed when the back door is open. Therefore, if the back door is open during camera optical axis adjustment in the registration settings, the message "Back door is open. Please close the back door before use." is displayed on the camera optical axis adjustment screen and the camera optical axis adjustment is cancelled.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>The back door lock assembly is connected to the instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU) by the vehicle wire harness.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000003NC100NX_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HYX00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E204699J01" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000003NC100NX_03" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HYY00000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When the battery terminal is disconnected, perform steering sensor neutral point memorization. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000GCY00LX"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Depending on the parts replaced or the work performed during inspection, registration and setting operations for other systems as well as the back guide monitor system may be necessary. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000002FZ603QX"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If registration/setting becomes necessary while proceeding with the inspection, perform the registration/setting work before proceeding to the next inspection step.  </ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000003NC100NX_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000003NC100NX_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HYZ00000">
<testtitle>TaSCAN ECU Data Monitor</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70201</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>ECU Data Monitor Inspection</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Start the engine and, using SST (TaSCAN), display the "ECU Data Monitor" screen following the screen display. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005KJ00MX"/>)</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<title>[Diagnosis menu screen: Body → Main Body → ECU Data Monitor]</title>
<tgroup cols="4">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.42in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.33in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.49in"/>
<colspec colname="COL4" colwidth="0.84in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Item Name</ptxt>
<ptxt>[Symbol]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Item Description/Display Range</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard Value</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Remarks</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Back Door Courtesy SW</ptxt>
<ptxt>[BCTY]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Displays back door courtesy light switch status</ptxt>
<ptxt>Display range: OFF/ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>OFF: Back door closed</ptxt>
<ptxt>ON: Back door open</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>-</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Open and close the back door, and check the ECU Data Monitor screen display in each state.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Display changes according to back door open/closed state</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003NC100NX_04_0002" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000003NC100NX_04_0004" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003NC100NX_04_0002">
<testtitle>Replace Navigation Receiver Assembly<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000001XG5006X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003NC100NX_04_0004" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HZ100000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Instrument Panel Junction Block Assembly (Main Body ECU) - Back Door Lock Assembly)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Pre-inspection Preparation  </ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Disconnect connector A of the instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU).</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Disconnect the back door lock assembly connector.</ptxt>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Resistance Inspection</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance of the wire harness between the instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU) and the back door lock assembly.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" align="left">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A7 (BCTY) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10 kΩ or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1 (ACT-) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A7(BCTY) - 3(D+)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003NC100NX_04_0005" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000003NC100NX_04_0008" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003NC100NX_04_0005" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HZ200000">
<testtitle>Inspect Back Door Lock Assembly</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Resistance Inspection</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B154882J14" width="2.775699831in" height="4.7836529in"/>
</figure>
<test2>
<ptxt>Set the back door lock assembly to the locked (full latch) state.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Using a screwdriver or equivalent, operate the latch of the back door lock assembly to set it to the locked (full latch) state.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the connector terminals.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" align="left">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1(ACT-) - 3(D+)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Locked (full latch) state</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10 kΩ or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Connect battery positive (+) to terminal 2 (ACT+) and battery negative (-) to terminal 1 (ACT-) of the connector, and set the back door lock assembly to the unlatched state.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the connector terminals.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" align="left">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1(ACT-) - 3(D+)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Unlatched state</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<table>
<title>Text in Illustrations</title>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="0.41in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.72in"/>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>*a</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry>
<ptxt>Locked (full latch) state</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>*b</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry>
<ptxt>Latch</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>*c</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry>
<ptxt>Unlatched state</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>*d</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry>
<ptxt>Connector Disconnected</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Back Door Lock Assembly)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003NC100NX_04_0006" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000003NC100NX_04_0009" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
